TICVAI should calculate the real usable cost.
Recipe Cost Revaluation
Authorized users shall be able to revalue every ingredient in a recipe using either the Last Receipt Rate or the Last 
Issue Rate.
Last Receipt Rate: the latest approved procurement rate at which the ingredient was received from a supplier.
Last Issue Rate: the latest approved rate at which the ingredient was issued from the store or warehouse to the 
kitchen or production location.
The selected valuation basis may be configured at company, outlet, recipe or ingredient level, subject to rolebased permissions and approval controls.
Before applying a revaluation, the system shall show the previous rate, proposed rate, effective date, source 
receipt or issue transaction, revised recipe cost, revised margin and affected products.
Revaluation shall support preview, approval, effective dating and bulk recalculation, while retaining the previous 
value and a complete audit trail. It shall not rewrite historical closed transactions unless an authorized financial 
adjustment process is used.

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 24
Nested Recipes / Sub-Recipes
A recipe shall be allowed as an ingredient or component within another recipe. For example, a Special Sauce 
recipe may be linked as a sub-recipe within a Burger recipe.
The parent recipe shall reference the approved sub-recipe version, required quantity and unit of measure, and 
shall automatically roll up the sub-recipe's ingredient cost, yield, wastage, allergens, nutrition and theoretical 
inventory consumption.
Changes to an active sub-recipe shall identify all affected parent recipes and products, recalculate their costs and 
margins, and follow the configured approval and effective-date workflow before publication.
The system shall prevent circular recipe links and provide a multi-level recipe-explosion view from the finished 
product down to the lowest-level ingredients.
Open Item Recipe and Receipt Linkage
The system shall provide an Open Item Recipe option for POS items that are not selected from a predefined 
product/PLU master record.
When an open item is sold, the cashier shall be able—or, where configured, be required—to link the sale to an 
approved open-item recipe or recipe template before settlement.
The open-item receipt line shall retain the entered item description, quantity, unit of measure, selling price, tax, 
linked recipe, calculated cost and margin, subject to permissions and approval thresholds.
The linked recipe shall drive ingredient-level theoretical consumption, costing, stock deduction, reporting and 
audit history. If no recipe is linked, the transaction shall be flagged as an exception for authorized review and 
reconciliation.
