SCREEN 3 — Order Firing & Course Management
Purpose
Provide advanced control over when kitchen preparation should begin.
This is particularly important for full-service restaurants, VIP dining, hospitality and event dining.
The system shall support four primary firing modes:
1. Fire & Forget
The complete order is automatically sent to the kitchen immediately after confirmation.
Example:
Quick-service restaurant order
→ Payment Confirmed
→ Automatically Fired
2. Hold & Fire
The order is received but preparation does not begin until an authorized employee releases it.
Example:
Main Course:
HELD
Waiter selects:
FIRE NOW
↓
Kitchen receives order.
3. Phased / Course Firing
Different courses are fired separately.
Example:

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 37
Starter
Fire Now ✓
Main Course
Held
Dessert
Held
When the guest finishes the starter:
Waiter selects:
Fire Main Course
4. Timed / Delayed Firing
Preparation begins automatically at a configured future time.
Example:
Pre-Order:
Guest Pickup:
13:00
Preparation Time:
15 minutes
TICVAI automatically fires:
12:45
Course Types
Configurable course types may include:
Drinks
Starter
Soup
Main Course
Side
Dessert
Coffee
Custom Course
