Architectural requirement
Development team should not create separate reservation engines for restaurants, VIP lounges, dining 
packages and event dining.
There should be a common Reservation & Capacity Engine:
Bookable Entity Capacity Availability Time Slot Guest Rules Reservation Payment/Deposit → → → → → → → →
Status
The F&B layer then adds:
Table Party Size Seating Preference Dining Duration Waitlist Service Table Turnover → → → → → →
This also aligns very well with the common Resource Engine architecture: restaurant tables can behave as 
bookable resources while the F&B module provides the specialized restaurant rules.
That approach will make it much easier later for TICVAI to support restaurant reservations bundled with tickets, 
events, memberships, VIP packages and experiences without creating separate booking logic for every product
type.

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 73
TICVAI F&B — BOARD 5
F&B Stock, Production, Replenishment & Operational Control — Scope of Work
1. Purpose
The F&B Stock, Production, Replenishment & Operational Control Board shall provide real-time management of 
ingredients, prepared items, consumables, production stock, outlet stock, wastage, stock counts, replenishment, 
internal transfers, availability, and operational food-safety controls across all Food & Beverage operations.
The Board shall connect F&B sales and production activities with TICVAI's shared Inventory & Procurement 
architecture without creating a separate inventory system inside the F&B module.
The core operational lifecycle shall be:
Sale / Forecast Recipe Consumption Theoretical Stock Actual Stock Variance Production → → → → →
Requirement Replenishment Outlet Availability → →
The module shall support:
 Restaurants
 Cafés
 Kiosks
 Food Trucks
 Bars
 VIP Lounges
 Event Catering
 Central Kitchens
 Commissaries
 Temporary Event Outlets

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 74
 Mobile F&B Operations
The Board shall support both outlet-level operations and central-kitchen production flows.
