ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENT
Board 5 shall not maintain a separate F&B inventory ledger.
There shall be one TICVAI inventory source of truth:
F&B Operational Event
↓
Recipe / Production Consumption Engine
↓
Shared Inventory Ledger
↓
Availability & Forecasting
↓
Replenishment
↓
Warehouse / Procurement
This same Shared Inventory Engine should later support F&B, Retail, Rental, operational supplies and other 
applicable TICVAI modules.
That gives TICVAI a clean architecture while Board 5 remains specialized enough to handle the operational 
realities of F&B: recipes, production, batches, yield, waste, expiry, 86 management and food safety.

