ADDITIONAL — STANDARD F&B POS 
FUNCTIONAL COVERAGE
Purpose. This amendment adds the POS operational functions identified in the F&B POS Standard Functions 
document that were missing or not stated explicitly in the backend structure. These requirements extend the 
existing six-board architecture and do not replace the more advanced capabilities already defined in the 
document.
Implementation principle. The functions below shall use the existing shared services for identity and access, 
payments, finance, CRM, inventory, approvals, audit, analytics and device management. Configuration belongs 
mainly to Board 1; kitchen execution to Board 3; table and guest service to Board 4; and reporting and intelligence
to Board 6.
