B. Board 1 Additions — User Access, Shift and Till Controls
Board 1 shall add a Cashier, Shift and Till Configuration area with the following standard functions:
 Configure mandatory opening cash balance/imprest by outlet, till, cashier and shift.
 Support cashier cash-in and cash-out with date/time, outlet, terminal, shift, opening balance, closing 
declaration and approval status.

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 128
 Track all transactions by cashier and shift and retain the applicable terminal and outlet context.
 Allow an authenticated cashier to suspend a POS session temporarily and resume it using password or 
approved authentication.
 Configure automatic return to the cashiering screen and timeout/session-lock rules.
 Configure a default outlet for authorized users while allowing permitted users to display and switch 
between available outlets.
 Display the active outlet, cashier, terminal and shift in the POS header.
 Provide user-level and shift-level reporting and a complete audit trail of opening, suspension, resumption 
and cash-out events.
C. Board 1 and Board 4 Additions — Check and Order Lifecycle
The Unified F&B Order Engine shall explicitly support the complete standard check lifecycle:
 Create a check with an automatically generated unique check number.
 Capture table number, cover count and server/waiter; allow configured defaults for quick-service and fastfood operations.
 Support table-service, counter, takeaway and delivery checks using the same order engine.
 Save an open check and retain all unsaved, saved, fired, printed and settled states.
 Recall a check by check number, table number or server number and show a selection list where several 
checks match.
 List all open checks for the current cashier and outlet, with permission-based access to other cashiers' 
checks.
 Preview the customer check before printing and support check inquiry by outlet and check number.
 Recall printed checks from the settlement workflow without duplicating or losing the original transaction 
reference.
 Print customer checks to configured continuous-feed, cut-sheet or receipt printers and prompt for 
manual paper insertion where required.
 Add individual items or numeric quantities, display description and price, scroll through the order and 
recalculate totals immediately.
 Support menu lists, category/submenu navigation, menu-item shortcut keys and configurable POS 
layouts already defined in Board 2.
D. Board 1 and Board 3 Additions — KOT Management
The existing KDS and printer-routing architecture shall include the following Kitchen Order Ticket controls:
 Automatically print or transmit a KOT when a check is saved or fired, according to the configured routing 
policy.
 On subsequent saves, send only newly added, changed or previously unsent items unless an authorized 
full reprint is requested.
 Maintain KOT history against the check and allow users to view all KOTs associated with a check or table.
 Display multiple KOTs separately, including sequence, station, print/fire time, user, status and reprint 
indicator.
 Reprint a KOT by outlet and check number, subject to permission, reason capture and audit logging.
 Print or display course-fire and course-hold instructions and reflect kitchen preparation status in the live 
table layout.
E. Board 1 and Board 4 Additions — Void and Item Transfer Controls
Void and transfer actions shall extend the existing approval and audit framework with explicit transaction 
behaviour:

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 129
 Void selected items, require a configured void reason and retain the original item plus a linked 
reversal/negative entry.
 Display a clear void indicator, recalculate the check balance and save or print the correction as configured.
 Void an entire check by reversing every original item, reducing the balance to zero and retaining the 
original and reversal audit chain.
 Report item voids and check voids by outlet, cashier, server, terminal, reason, approver, date and value.
 Move selected items from a source check to an existing or newly created destination check.
 Locate the destination by table, check or server and display all matches where the reference is not 
unique.
 Update both source and destination totals atomically and retain user, reason, approval and crossreferenced check numbers.
F. Board 3 and Board 4 Additions — Cover, Course and Service Status
The existing course, kitchen and table-service functionality shall be expanded or clarified as follows:
 Assign ordered items to individual covers/guests and show the cover number against each item.
 Allow cover-wise and course-wise ordering within the same check.
 Create multiple courses, tag items by course, prompt for the first course and manually fire or hold later 
courses.
 Mark one or more items as serviced and display the service status against each item and in the table 
layout.
 Provide configurable colour-coded table states including vacant, opened/no order, preparing, partially 
ready, ready/serviced and cleaning.
 Provide a visible status legend and permit authorized configuration of table-state colours.
 Open the check and KOT history directly from the table map, including separate views for multiple KOTs.
G. Board 4 Additions — Delivery Outlet and Guest Profile Functions
Delivery outlets shall use the shared TICVAI Guest Profile/CRM while supporting the following POS workflow:
 Configure an outlet as delivery-enabled and permit telephone number to act as the primary order lookup 
instead of table number.
 Search existing guests by telephone number and prompt to create a profile when no match is found.
 Capture guest name, full address, multiple contact numbers, birthday, anniversary, guest class and 
preferences.
 Edit the guest profile subject to CRM permissions and data-protection controls.
 Automatically retrieve returning-guest details and display previous orders and the items within a selected 
order.
 Filter or group order history by outlet and other permitted dimensions.
 Use the standard order, KOT, settlement and reporting workflows for delivery checks.
H. Board 1 and Board 4 Additions — Happy Hour, Discounts, Tips, Tax 
and Settlement
The pricing and settlement design shall explicitly include these standard operational controls:
 Permit authorized manual start/end of happy-hour pricing, display a header indicator and apply 
configured happy-hour prices only to subsequently posted items.
 Configure whether manual happy-hour switching is allowed and report normal-hour and happy-hour 
sales separately.
 Support cash settlement with exact payment, over-tender and automatic change calculation.

TICVAI / F&B BACKEND STRUCTURE MODULE
CONFIDENTIAL | 130
 Display configured card types and capture only PCI-compliant payment references or masked/tokenized 
details required by the payment integration.
 Support room, guest, special, group, corporate and city-ledger account charges where integrated, 
including room/account inquiry and advanced search.
 Support partial and mixed-tender settlement, with the outstanding balance recalculated after each 
tender.
 Add, confirm and remove a manual tip before final settlement and include it in the check total and tip 
reporting.
 Apply predefined or ad hoc percentage discounts to the entire check, all revenue heads or selected 
heads/categories.
 Capture guest and membership references where required, remove an applied discount and recalculate 
the balance.
 Apply configured full or partial tax-exemption categories and recalculate the check balance while 
retaining approval and audit details.
I. Board 4 Addition — Standard Split-Check Behaviour
In addition to split-by-guest and split-by-item, the system shall support the following standard split-check controls:
 Split one check into multiple independent checks, with a configurable limit that may be restricted to the 
number of covers.
 Divide the balance equally by default and allow authorized custom amounts.
 Validate that the total of all split checks exactly equals the original balance.
 Recall and settle each split check independently using different payment methods.
 Maintain split-check lineage and separate reporting while preventing unsupported changes to the 
original check after completion of the split.
J. Board 6 Additions — Standard POS Report Catalogue
Board 6 shall include, or source through the common reporting layer, the following standard operational reports:
 Cashier reports: Shift End, Daily Summary, Item Sales, Open Checks, Check Inquiry, Reprint KOT and 
Reprint Check.
 Daily reports: Day Summary, Settlement, Item Sales, Open Checks, Sales by Check, Settlement by Check 
and Covers.
 Control reports: Void Items, Void Checks, Discounts, Shift End Summary, Tax-Exempted Checks, 100% 
Discounted Checks, Discounts by Category, Authorization, Cash Drop, Tax Scroll, Tips Scroll and Reprint 
Check Logs.
 MIS reports: Charge Summary, Covers Summary, Item Sales Summary, Top 10 Best/Worst Selling Items, 
Item Sales by Day of Week, Contact List, MIS Void Items, NC Check Detail and Loyalty Card Details.
 To-date MIS summaries: Item Sales, Charge, Covers, Settlement, Discount and Tax, with MTD and YTD 
values where applicable.
 Report filters: date/date range, time range, tenant, company, venue, outlet, cashier, server, shift, terminal,
settlement method, item group, item, product type, menu, channel, normal/happy hour and 
inclusion/exclusion of open checks.
 Report output to screen, configured printer and approved export formats, subject to role-based 
permissions.
 Item Sales reporting shall include quantity, sales value and potential/theoretical cost.